[{:db/id "q-49902/selection/103f342561c3867b98d73a5327b733de3639d7b331493b438aeda6c76346df6e" :answer/id #uuid "d994a69f-f77a-577b-a7ed-c79e3e4a31d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49902/selection/27bbe25ea62c122580310e0bb3cd388502a2c8df93ec8dea73ab4fb3951acc57" :answer/id #uuid "a87e02af-54ae-55ef-b15b-efee1401452b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49902/selection/6a16f0cde29613461ca2482afb5d4aaaa7d0f707437cb28da66847c63ebd136c" :answer/id #uuid "58126e72-b979-5d73-916c-81500fa394ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49902/selection/f709b66aaf61fda24138ce300ee28d3014ecefe6030679beabf67345750721b1" :answer/id #uuid "f8b4d31f-9a9c-5038-ae39-809d7ff481ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49902/selection/7f99299d703b87d8490a9c1563683f3e83204babcdc442b96125f5384804c055" :answer/id #uuid "aaef68f1-372c-5f9f-a35d-3d21f85080f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49902/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe59d3fe-bee7-5f4b-b675-cb8f51b9df58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49902/selection/103f342561c3867b98d73a5327b733de3639d7b331493b438aeda6c76346df6e" :answer-field/choices ["q-49902/selection/103f342561c3867b98d73a5327b733de3639d7b331493b438aeda6c76346df6e" "q-49902/selection/27bbe25ea62c122580310e0bb3cd388502a2c8df93ec8dea73ab4fb3951acc57" "q-49902/selection/6a16f0cde29613461ca2482afb5d4aaaa7d0f707437cb28da66847c63ebd136c" "q-49902/selection/f709b66aaf61fda24138ce300ee28d3014ecefe6030679beabf67345750721b1" "q-49902/selection/7f99299d703b87d8490a9c1563683f3e83204babcdc442b96125f5384804c055"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49902" :question/id #uuid "0f4beeb0-a230-5a24-9f4a-0465c9611ed3" :question/math-academy-id "q-49902" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{4x}{(x-2)^{2}}\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x}{(x-2)^{2}} & =\\frac{A}{(x-2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-2)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n4x=A(x-2)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2) & =A(2-2)+B \\\\ 8 & =0+B \\\\ B & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0) & =A(0-2)+B \\\\ 0 & =-2A+B \\\\ 0 & =-2A+8 \\\\ A & =\\frac{8}{2} \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{4}{(x-2)}+\\frac{8}{(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{4x}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(\\frac{4}{(x-2)}+\\frac{8}{(x-2)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x+8{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|{|}_{3}^{4}+8(-\\frac{1}{x-2}){|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3-2|)+8(-\\frac{1}{4-2}+\\frac{1}{3-2}) \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3-2|)+8(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49902/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05dd17d8-4170-5392-89e7-7547184b8556"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49902"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348426/field-1/b8b44fe991595c2815fe7866182a4355f303afb0f562c6dddac363696fa29046" :answer/id #uuid "e852ee88-acdf-5dcd-b07e-b239ab122820" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(6)-\\ln(5)-\\frac{2}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348426/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0552638d-bdad-58ba-be81-ace0a565fd45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348426/field-1/b8b44fe991595c2815fe7866182a4355f303afb0f562c6dddac363696fa29046" :answer-field/choices ["q-348426/field-1/b8b44fe991595c2815fe7866182a4355f303afb0f562c6dddac363696fa29046"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348426" :question/id #uuid "bcd59b71-fa7a-559a-acad-1450e2b093f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-348426" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+5}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+5)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\nx+1=A(x+5)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-5,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5+1 & =A(-5+5)+B \\\\ B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+1 & =A(0+5)-4 \\\\ 1 & =5A-4 \\\\ 5A & =5 \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x+5}-\\frac{4}{(x+5)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{x+5}-\\frac{4}{(x+5)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{4}{x+5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+5|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+5|)+(\\frac{4}{1+5}-\\frac{4}{0+5}) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)+(\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{4}{5}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{5})-\\frac{2}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348426/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05dd17d8-4170-5392-89e7-7547184b8556"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348426"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346710/field-1/5887278284d58b91a61540b9e0646bbe55a2b66dc14b4eaa079dac211cccee95" :answer/id #uuid "f0d930c3-673d-53db-9ab2-8865c64a1066" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\ln(2)-\\ln(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346710/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "64d86e5b-7946-5f65-a9c7-4262a6ecdbf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346710/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "82d45098-6cdb-536b-9dcd-f3aa38454270" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346710/field-1/5887278284d58b91a61540b9e0646bbe55a2b66dc14b4eaa079dac211cccee95" :answer-field/choices ["q-346710/field-1/5887278284d58b91a61540b9e0646bbe55a2b66dc14b4eaa079dac211cccee95" "q-346710/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346710" :question/id #uuid "cd5af66b-b2ec-535a-9378-0690b5352eba" :question/math-academy-id "q-346710" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{x+2}{(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-4}+\\frac{B}{(x-4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-4)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\nx+2=A(x-4)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4+2 & =A(4-4)+B \\\\ B & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+2 & =A(0-4)+6 \\\\ 2 & =-4A+6 \\\\ 4A & =4 \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x-4}+\\frac{6}{(x-4)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{x+2}{(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{1}{x-4}+\\frac{6}{(x-4)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x+6{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|\\,{|}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{6}{x-4}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-4|)-(\\frac{6}{2-4}-\\frac{6}{1-4}) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-(-3-(-2)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-346710/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05dd17d8-4170-5392-89e7-7547184b8556"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346710"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115323/selection/fb13f3a3ef1255e9a120764655c4c18dbd0945be6ef8af78774a2e72e1f2a912" :answer/id #uuid "bd57a677-3b5e-57f3-b4a5-16de5b56b755" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115323/selection/066d29bf0279c0dcc9773848d7c37f62f4816f6391802c36f026f8c67f44f747" :answer/id #uuid "b87928e3-ae73-5916-9b48-de246231c1f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115323/selection/abc9df07e920c6432f207ddb835700c8bd2d635a8fcc570a119190d2c7a68c7d" :answer/id #uuid "c7ed51fe-785c-56dd-a205-9b6ed0e3f36a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{4}{x-2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115323/selection/c6fed8baf29ed045475aa9cb2c609fbea601a32f492d1a318d3939259c06f731" :answer/id #uuid "28251d54-0ca6-5844-a528-f9e2a7d1d410" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{4}{x-2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115323/selection/5fcc1919367bcba6897a971607a727fb8ddec22ce91cfdfe30406ca4b2d6316e" :answer/id #uuid "063b8da2-643e-508b-beae-2acb0dd19215" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115323/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6105b939-e78e-5141-8c85-e6dc7821ec4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115323/selection/fb13f3a3ef1255e9a120764655c4c18dbd0945be6ef8af78774a2e72e1f2a912" :answer-field/choices ["q-115323/selection/fb13f3a3ef1255e9a120764655c4c18dbd0945be6ef8af78774a2e72e1f2a912" "q-115323/selection/066d29bf0279c0dcc9773848d7c37f62f4816f6391802c36f026f8c67f44f747" "q-115323/selection/abc9df07e920c6432f207ddb835700c8bd2d635a8fcc570a119190d2c7a68c7d" "q-115323/selection/c6fed8baf29ed045475aa9cb2c609fbea601a32f492d1a318d3939259c06f731" "q-115323/selection/5fcc1919367bcba6897a971607a727fb8ddec22ce91cfdfe30406ca4b2d6316e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115323" :question/id #uuid "121bc432-4485-5cd3-bccf-f598e063c559" :question/math-academy-id "q-115323" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{(x-2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-2)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n4x-10=A(x-2)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)-10 & =A(2-2)+B \\\\ -2 & =0+B \\\\ B & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)-10 & =A(0-2)+B \\\\ -10 & =-2A-2 \\\\ -2A & =-8 \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{4}{(x-2)}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4x-10}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{(x-2)}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-2(-\\frac{1}{x-2})+C \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115323/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05dd17d8-4170-5392-89e7-7547184b8556"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115323"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348350/field-1/e7add6407c394892f10f4290b30c29c251e2c16e7b7243513b70a140fb73fd4b" :answer/id #uuid "fb88a5b0-67c9-5ca1-b212-be1346dc1e88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(4)-\\ln(5)+\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348350/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c1f80e9-ddac-59be-9b61-a84416ac794c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348350/field-1/e7add6407c394892f10f4290b30c29c251e2c16e7b7243513b70a140fb73fd4b" :answer-field/choices ["q-348350/field-1/e7add6407c394892f10f4290b30c29c251e2c16e7b7243513b70a140fb73fd4b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348350" :question/id #uuid "9c220092-846f-5eac-8c3f-776c702f7e39" :question/math-academy-id "q-348350" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+3}{(x-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{(x-5)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-5}+\\frac{B}{(x-5)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-5)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\nx+3=A(x-5)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=5,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5+3 & =A(5-5)+B \\\\ B & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+3 & =A(0-5)+8 \\\\ 3 & =-5A+8 \\\\ 5A & =5 \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{(x-5)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x-5}+\\frac{8}{(x-5)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+3}{(x-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{x-5}+\\frac{8}{(x-5)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x-5}\\,\\text{d}x+8{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-5|\\,{|}_{0}^{1}-\\frac{8}{x-5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-5|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0-5|)-(\\frac{8}{1-5}-\\frac{8}{0-5}) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)-(-2-(-\\frac{8}{5})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{5})+\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348350/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05dd17d8-4170-5392-89e7-7547184b8556"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348350"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186068946 :question/answer-fields 17592186065470] {:db/id "q-11340/selection/ma-v1/4b387370fb036