e :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11340/selection/ma-v1/4b387370fb03647340f4d9f425a6cf9b7d11e3b43fa1ab97639e7bd95be4d8f8/08cfa591ca8ee0b5f2f10ac5b2a5d053e370dc87a4f469c22a2f562f556a2e13" :answer-field/choices ["q-11340/selection/ma-v1/4b387370fb03647340f4d9f425a6cf9b7d11e3b43fa1ab97639e7bd95be4d8f8/08cfa591ca8ee0b5f2f10ac5b2a5d053e370dc87a4f469c22a2f562f556a2e13" "q-11340/selection/ma-v1/4b387370fb03647340f4d9f425a6cf9b7d11e3b43fa1ab97639e7bd95be4d8f8/fddea3e86af80c631bad9b2ca48a4283df02f65ba2d1a82fba4120fa05f5007f" "q-11340/selection/ma-v1/4b387370fb03647340f4d9f425a6cf9b7d11e3b43fa1ab97639e7bd95be4d8f8/1c81ac93abb1289e71ab44415bd5fc4db6674a2d75cd823d006240747ad1cd04" "q-11340/selection/ma-v1/4b387370fb03647340f4d9f425a6cf9b7d11e3b43fa1ab97639e7bd95be4d8f8/9467ece7f4bb65fa17e608d18a1be353dca4b1d2d46e61d740b70e4340c77c36" "q-11340/selection/ma-v1/4b387370fb03647340f4d9f425a6cf9b7d11e3b43fa1ab97639e7bd95be4d8f8/1d900425ca368eb5676462f30873d08678062122be7d2cb42f89dd53708cd25f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11340"] :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-3)}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+2)^{2}(x-3)$ and get\n\n$$\n5x+35=A(x+2)(x-3)+B(x-3)+C(x+2)^{2}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $C$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-2)+35 & =A(-2+2)(-2-3)+B(-2-3)+C(-2+2)^{2} \\\\ -10+35 & =B(-5) \\\\ B & =\\frac{25}{-5} \\\\ B & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(3)+35 & =A(3+2)(3-3)+B(3-3)+C(3+2)^{2} \\\\ 15+35 & =C{(5)}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{50}{25} \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known values of $B$ and $C,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(0)+35 & =A(0+2)(0-3)+B(0-3)+C(0+2)^{2} \\\\ 35 & =-6A-3B+4C \\\\ 35 & =-6A-3(-5)+4(2) \\\\ 35 & =-6A+23 \\\\ 6A & =-35+23 \\\\ A & =\\frac{-12}{6} \\\\ A & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}=-\\frac{2}{(x+2)}-\\frac{5}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x-3)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x+35}{(x+2)^{2}(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{2}{(x+2)}-\\frac{5}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x-3)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{5}{x+2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11340/selection/ma-v1/4b387370fb03647340f4d9f425a6cf9b7d11e3b43fa1ab97639e7bd95be4d8f8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-11373/selection/c087ee4b9081ded2223a008315783e2b339443a1f186d35ea8263714662a6ff7" :answer/id #uuid "d0822243-4d73-54a6-9195-4a9724fe3e2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|-\\frac{3}{2x+3}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11373/selection/3738d8407e888876b79730c98a13a961b112fd5275181c6c24ab4e28e0e35229" :answer/id #uuid "38ab01e4-c77e-5e40-bc9f-a5a2b819ffd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+\\frac{2}{2x+3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11373/selection/426d12fe44598e3ad9cc6007b893e1ff93c4ce1dfd30e899581653fcd821849e" :answer/id #uuid "76b2fec1-8cf1-5057-bce1-1f0399ad1d94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+\\frac{3}{2x+3}-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11373/selection/42232bbaf0ce3f96587fd0fa2e8b39fdb11ab1629d26657c3eda3e5ca6fc8fb0" :answer/id #uuid "d71b72d9-84d3-5862-8d6b-1d324da25f77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|-\\frac{1}{2x+3}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11373/selection/3ddacd27a9728a02a8c0c894224c4a963ce52ba20195de246ff0479c0b768064" :answer/id #uuid "c77abbfa-a836-5179-8fdf-5d99e465c0c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+\\frac{1}{2x+3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11373/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ccfc7130-a98e-57de-9f14-3ddc1dffd4bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11373/selection/42232bbaf0ce3f96587fd0fa2e8b39fdb11ab1629d26657c3eda3e5ca6fc8fb0" :answer-field/choices ["q-11373/selection/c087ee4b9081ded2223a008315783e2b339443a1f186d35ea8263714662a6ff7" "q-11373/selection/3738d8407e888876b79730c98a13a961b112fd5275181c6c24ab4e28e0e35229" "q-11373/selection/426d12fe44598e3ad9cc6007b893e1ff93c4ce1dfd30e899581653fcd821849e" "q-11373/selection/42232bbaf0ce3f96587fd0fa2e8b39fdb11ab1629d26657c3eda3e5ca6fc8fb0" "q-11373/selection/3ddacd27a9728a02a8c0c894224c4a963ce52ba20195de246ff0479c0b768064"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11373" :question/id #uuid "a314e13d-b287-542f-9d01-bb5a501b5ab7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11373" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{14{x}^{2}+47x+42}{(2x+3)^{2}(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14{x}^{2}+47x+42}{(2x+3)^{2}(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(2x+3)}+\\frac{B}{(2x+3)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+3)}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(2x+3)^{2}(x+3)$ and get\n\n$$\n14{x}^{2}+47x+42=A(2x+3)(x+3)+B(x+3)+C(2x+3)^{2}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-\\frac{3}{2},$ we can eliminate $A$ and $C$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14{(-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+47(-\\frac{3}{2})+42 & =A(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)(-\\frac{3}{2}+3) \\\\  & +B(-\\frac{3}{2}+3)+C{(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{63}{2}-\\frac{141}{2}+42 & =B(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{63-141+84}{2} & =B(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ B & =-\\frac{12}{6} \\\\ B & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14(-3)^{2}+47(-3)+42 & =A(2(-3)+3)(-3+3)+B(-3+3)+C(2(-3)+3)^{2} \\\\ 126-141+42 & =C{(-3)}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{27}{9} \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known values of $B$ and $C,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14({0}^{2})+47(0)+42 & =A(2(0)+3)(0+3)+B(0+3)+C(2(0)+3)^{2} \\\\ 42 & =9A+3B+9C \\\\ 42 & =9A+3(2)+9(3) \\\\ 42 & =9A+33 \\\\ 9A & =42-33 \\\\ A & =\\frac{9}{9} \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{14{x}^{2}+47x+42}{(2x+3)^{2}(x+3)}=\\frac{1}{(2x+3)}+\\frac{2}{(2x+3)^{2}}+\\frac{3}{(x+3)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{14{x}^{2}+47x+42}{(2x+3)^{2}(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{(2x+3)}+\\frac{2}{(2x+3)^{2}}+\\frac{3}{(x+3)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{(2x+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|-\\frac{1}{2x+3}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11373/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68e983da-1f69-5be1-8034-9422a84ce6be"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11373"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49785/selection/9ebf66d70dcc11ae2c41f4a86b5f72a782dab061bfee584fc5f05fba56fc48d2" :answer/id #uuid "f5883cd4-3498-55c5-8a68-4af727b1a500" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49785/selection/b9f4857f715b3ea4dd947d132e23a0c39ffb7b0a531c0d908d7b07baab01fd2a" :answer/id #uuid "183d8c82-a5ec-5886-ab3f-7c95273e4857" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2x}+\\frac{6}{23}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49785/selection/1b5bd77510463c0abdb669bb30c2d39c419146e1fa44728680ad5544fb33acd1" :answer/id #uuid "c723e5ef-65d6-5e48-a38b-01f857c855fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{23}{6}\\frac{1}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49785/selection/abd6096c6db3fc728ec21307a2b733b456100204dca2c17418cb2bca292d2737" :answer/id #uuid "919a00ab-be13-5d98-bb76-9364a21eda90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{5}{3x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49785/selection/6ba0955651d319014087792fc9209f17ed561ea056531b1319b94adae67c2a59" :answer/id #uuid "ce6cdf46-25f3-5209-b7ef-e0a36cea9655" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{23}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49785/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "38348bb2-28f3-54cf-a187-5e498cfc4669" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49785/selection/6ba0955651d319014087792fc9209f17ed561ea056531b1319b94adae67c2a59" :answer-field/choices ["q-49785/selection/9ebf66d70dcc11ae2c41f4a86b5f72a782dab061bfee584fc5f05fba56fc48d2" "q-49785/selection/b9f4857f715b3ea4dd947d132e23a0c39ffb7b0a531c0d908d7b07baab01fd2a" "q-49785/selection/1b5bd77510463c0abdb669bb30c2d39c419146e1fa44728680ad5544fb33acd1" "q-49785/selection/abd6096c6db3fc728ec21307a2b733b456100204dca2c17418cb2bca292d2737" "q-49785/selection/6ba0955651d319014087792fc9209f17ed561ea056531b1319b94adae67c2a59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49785" :question/id #uuid "145e4701-d43b-5056-a42b-a1c651706ffd" :question/math-academy-id "q-49785" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+6}{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}=-\\frac{4}{3x}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{23}{3(2x+3)},\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\int \\frac{5{x}^{2}+6}{(2x+3){x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We rewrite our integral and integrate term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5{x}^{2}+6}{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{4}{3x}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{23}{3(2x+3)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{23}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{23}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-49785/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68e983da-1f69-5be1-8034-9422a84ce6be"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49785"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348473/field-1/5d5c04bbf7550c788a8ae7f62e47175d949a72957d1e43e8939c6068aa040689" :answer/id #uuid "a23ce9b4-4fa6-53f0-a3c5-7ee5114d937f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\ln(3)+\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348473/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "94d2adad-5115-5fb1-abac-1a26125f244e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348473/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a84a7c1a-381f-5ecf-8c7a-54d3630dcb7d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348473/field-1/5d5c04bbf7550c788a8ae7f62e47175d949a72957d1e43e8939c6068aa040689" :answer-field/choices ["q-348473/field-1/5d5c04bbf7550c788a8ae7f62e47175d949a72957d1e43e8939c6068aa040689" "q-348473/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348473" :question/id #uuid "442912a0-d2e7-5b68-8200-12d7316f04a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-348473" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-4}+\\frac{C}{(x-4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x(x-4)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n8-x=A(x-4)^{2}+Bx(x-4)+Cx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and $C$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-0 & =A(0-4)^{2}+B(0)(0-4)+C(0) \\\\ 8 & =16A \\\\ A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-4 & =A(4-4)^{2}+B(4)(4-4)+C(4) \\\\ 4 & =4C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1$ and substituting the known values of $A$ and $C,$ we can solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-1 & =A(1-4)^{2}+B(1)(1-4)+C(1) \\\\ 7 & =9A-3B+C \\\\ 7 & =9(\\frac{1}{2})-3B+1 \\\\ B & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2x}-\\frac{1}{2(x-4)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{1}{2x}-\\frac{1}{2(x-4)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|\\,{|}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|\\,{|}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{1}{x-4}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348473/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68e983da-1f69-5be1-8034-9422a84ce6be"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348473"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11369/selection/5b037478ee3b2dbf3968b73f5a9f6be727f2c01c67753f64abad9b717880e225" :answer/id #uuid "fc68f114-a145-5857-ab06-d0c90378d2c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|-\\frac{2}{1-x}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11369/selection/eb82453d2641c31e914c5a61583fce61f29ff72e84d6091176b0c578e2cdd83c" :answer/id #uuid "6a6d9360-bbce-55bc-bd32-24cc5016c05f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|+\\frac{3}{1-x}-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11369/selection/85f2ab2fb47c53d7a7dac254cf38bf901844716328e8ab16946f0c89fd1de9f2" :answer/id #uuid "178cb0a4-8945-594e-8f8b-60ef6c57aafe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|-\\frac{3}{1-x}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11369/selection/9fb09e21d7d3326bc390d4c2eb732e168602de00d065a639e2f945b7b116a839" :answer/id #uuid "5a724608-8e02-50d7-9012-c0bdce32187e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|-\\frac{2}{1-x}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11369/selection/f9ff747fc16edb4cbaced08b75161a23f746a81d716ace3e81db1ddd0ff859c9" :answer/id #uuid "59a2f51a-8ea5-5688-b3a0-71a8a6684752" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|+\\frac{3}{1-x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11369/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "220e86b4-f643-5ab4-a2b9-e3f7771ec7c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11369/selection/f9ff747fc16edb4cbaced08b75161a23f746a81d716ace3e81db1ddd0ff859c9" :answer-field/choices ["q-11369/selection/5b037478ee3b2dbf3968b73f5a9f6be727f2c01c67753f64abad9b717880e225" "q-11369/selection/eb82453d2641c31e914c5a61583fce61f29ff72e84d6091176b0c578e2cdd83c" "q-11369/selection/85f2ab2fb47c53d7a7dac254cf38bf901844716328e8ab16946f0c89fd1de9f2" "q-11369/selection/9fb09e21d7d3326bc390d4c2eb732e168602de00d065a639e2f945b7b116a839" "q-11369/selection/f9ff747fc16edb4cbaced08b75161a23f746a81d716ace3e81db1ddd0ff859c9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11369" :question/id #uuid "42759d43-e843-516a-a952-88c7ffb6134c" :question/math-academy-id "q-11369" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{-9x+27}{(1-x)^{2}(x+5)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{-9x+27}{(1-x)^{2}(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{(1-x)}+\\frac{B}{(1-x)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(1-x)^{2}(x+5)$ and get\n\n$$\n-9x+27=A(1-x)(x+5)+B(x+5)+C(1-x)^{2}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $C$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9(1)+27 & =A(1-1)(1+5)+B(1+5)+C(1-1)^{2} \\\\ -9+27 & =B(6) \\\\ B & =\\frac{18}{6} \\\\ B & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-5,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9(-5)+27 & =A(1-(-5))(-5+5)+B(-5+5)+C(1-(-5))^{2} \\\\ -45+27 & =C{(6)}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{72}{36} \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known values of $B$ and $C,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9(0)+27 & =A(1-0)(0+5)+B(0+5)+C(1-0)^{2} \\\\ 27 & =5A+5B+C \\\\ 27 & =5A+5(3)+2 \\\\ 27 & =5A+17 \\\\ 5A & =27-17 \\\\ A & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\ A & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-9x+27}{(1-x)^{2}(x+5)}=\\frac{2}{(1-x)}+\\frac{3}{(1-x)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-9x+27}{(1-x)^{2}(x+5)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{(1-x)}+\\frac{3}{(1-x)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|+\\frac{3}{1-x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11369/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68e983da-1f69-5be1-8034-9422a84ce6be"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11369"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348521/field-1/e11f43796a93284d49deb787a70e70a6bc4b4c3b7166bd8b046525fb6bec4654" :answer/id #uuid "b3c36196-c673-5b59-93f2-909cd5d56d93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(4)-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348521/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dededca6-bf82-57a0-b7cf-d7a877f561e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348521/field-1/e11f43796a93284d49deb787a70e70a6bc4b4c3b7166bd8b046525fb6bec4654" :answer-field/choices ["q-348521/field-1/e11f43796a93284d49deb787a70e70a6bc4b4c3b7166bd8b046525fb6bec4654"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348521" :question/id #uuid "a562073f-476e-5423-a33d-a22e612a68b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-348521" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{2-x}{{x}^{2}-12x+36}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-x}{{x}^{2}-12x+36}=\\frac{2-x}{(x-6)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-x}{(x-6)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-6}+\\frac{B}{(x-6)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-6)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n2-x=A(x-6)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=6,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-6 & =A(6-6)+B \\\\ B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-0 & =A(0-6)-4 \\\\ 2 & =-6A-4 \\\\ A & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-x}{(x-6)^{2}}=-\\frac{1}{x-6}-\\frac{4}{(x-6)^{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{2-x}{(x-6)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}(-\\frac{1}{x-6}-\\frac{4}{(x-6)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{x-6}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{(x-6)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-6|\\,{|}_{2}^{5}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{x-6}\\,{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)+4(-1-(-\\frac{1}{4})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+4(-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348521/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf7f11d9-6aa8-5922-a5fa-89f7dba66644"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348521"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348617/field-1/d03f7b312c57880b03ee9e24d0c440fcd35433fff872c21302698d239e9a5af7" :answer/id #uuid "d18e8131-971f-5aa5-923b-0169ac81f6d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\ln(2)-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348617/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "9e3a673b-e8e4-5aa8-9bfd-aee89ad5dc50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348617/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b760fa9-8473-53aa-bd5b-e6fb7a2c0288" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348617/field-1/d03f7b312c57880b03ee9e24d0c440fcd35433fff872c21302698d239e9a5af7" :answer-field/choices ["q-348617/field-1/d03f7b312c57880b03ee9e24d0c440fcd35433fff872c21302698d239e9a5af7" "q-348617/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348617" :question/id #uuid "ae9f08bc-be36-5848-9bd0-b853f4db7daf" :question/math-academy-id "q-348617" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}+8x+16}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}+8x+16}=\\frac{3x+7}{(x+4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+7}{(x+4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+4}+\\frac{B}{(x+4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+4)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n3x+7=A(x+4)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-4)+7 & =A(-4+4)+B \\\\ B & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)+7 & =A(0+4)-5 \\\\ 7 & =4A-5 \\\\ A & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+7}{(x+4)^{2}}=\\frac{3}{x+4}-\\frac{5}{(x+4)^{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{3x+7}{(x+4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-6}^{-5}(\\frac{3}{x+4}-\\frac{5}{(x+4)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{-6}^{-5}+5\\cdot \\frac{1}{x+4}\\,{|}_{-6}^{-5} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)+5(-1-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})+5(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348617/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf7f11d9-6aa8-5922-a5fa-89f7dba66644"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348617"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115537/selection/747d6ce357606dd720c00e7ff5be7b55e079b292dbf0ac2a37b0dfcac6892285" :answer/id #uuid "b9a3c53d-a365-5c65-98de-1cbbb15ad00a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{1}{x-2}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115537/selection/b35dfab35f0ab313379658768a42c66dfb449f2a979e39a3bca4f92ff876c653" :answer/id #uuid "dfa78d58-4669-520a-8109-bf6693cb281f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{1}{x-2}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115537/selection/b6e600265a794ecceb9ef7e6062068a9868d322d23d96ad78b536023b055c99a" :answer/id #uuid "0571ef11-9ad6-582a-9561-ab8ab4deab95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115537/selection/cda5723ede7fe9b4457faf4957cfafcbc398017d462502835eeb9eef15cdf89d" :answer/id #uuid "c242b7a4-a488-5cb7-83ac-33ed15177ff2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{4}{x-2}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115537/selection/5e62464058410f8a1e5cdae420a7e8e5372bf9b81e38d3d9343473336e8f7cd1" :answer/id #uuid "f85b8fb5-6432-588a-8182-63109a019a33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{3}{x-2}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115537/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8043fe4d-6bef-52e3-b006-8b072412feef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115537/selection/b6e600265a794ecceb9ef7e6062068a9868d322d23d96ad78b536023b055c99a" :answer-field/choices ["q-115537/selection/747d6ce357606dd720c00e7ff5be7b55e079b292dbf0ac2a37b0dfcac6892285" "q-115537/selection/b35dfab35f0ab313379658768a42c66dfb449f2a979e39a3bca4f92ff876c653" "q-115537/selection/b6e600265a794ecceb9ef7e6062068a9868d322d23d96ad78b536023b055c99a" "q-115537/selection/cda5723ede7fe9b4457faf4957cfafcbc398017d462502835eeb9eef15cdf89d" "q-115537/selection/5e62464058410f8a1e5cdae420a7e8e5372bf9b81e38d3d9343473336e8f7cd1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115537" :question/id #uuid "7ae7adfa-d253-53d5-ac7b-8d1dff4b65e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-115537" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+4x}=\\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{x(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{x(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-2}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x(x-2)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-12x+4=A(x-2)^{2}+Bx(x-2)+Cx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)^{2}-12(2)+4 & =A(2-2)^{2}+B(2)(2-2)+C(2) \\\\ -4 & =2C \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and $C$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}-12(0)+4 & =A(0-2)^{2}+B(0)(0-2)+C(0) \\\\ 4 & =4A \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=1$ and substituting the known values of $A$ and $C,$ we can solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(1)^{2}-12(1)+4 & =A(1-2)^{2}+B(1)(1-2)+C(1) \\\\ -4 & =A-B+C \\\\ -4 & =1-B+(-2) \\\\ -3 & =-B \\\\ B & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+4x}=\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{3}{x-2}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-12x+4}{{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{3}{x-2}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{2}{x-2}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-115537/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf7f11d9-6aa8-5922-a5fa-89f7dba66644"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115537"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-3612/selection/2101964c5e393c91bd6e89357c7e5f6dcaae2de1a8525711a36acac9327c5391" :answer/id #uuid "e143f29f-94b2-52da-918d-7f17de7556a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|+\\frac{9}{t+1}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3612/selection/965d5b44bd683e641b885d6c980fb57d353493f7145dc5da4741c9cd7a3ac72b" :answer/id #uuid "9d9dcecf-b626-5f68-a905-9571dacd9e8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|+\\frac{9}{t+1}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3612/selection/7c50e7c95f8d57e8c2cf800424231b37ee9844a3458953ffca6278685bf63459" :answer/id #uuid "e6dadb2c-c0ef-5696-b687-585997eedb31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|-\\frac{9}{t+1}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3612/selection/4483b951f4ebc1f59c02791c83d8c6eb30900b71491c8259ba655efdc2e63d22" :answer/id #uuid "fed245c7-2d13-5533-b747-3df5d69d3b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|-\\frac{2}{t+1}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3612/selection/ba537c76c05c73718ad3b01ea2b4a74658881a86190c8376c56e2027bb244c7f" :answer/id #uuid "05825022-1d62-5bc3-a9a8-4bdc604a2133" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|-\\frac{1}{t+1}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3612/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8af71650-5e17-5946-89ae-00df8d17eae4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-3612/selection/7c50e7c95f8d57e8c2cf800424231b37ee9844a3458953ffca6278685bf63459" :answer-field/choices ["q-3612/selection/2101964c5e393c91bd6e89357c7e5f6dcaae2de1a8525711a36acac9327c5391" "q-3612/selection/965d5b44bd683e641b885d6c980fb57d353493f7145dc5da4741c9cd7a3ac72b" "q-3612/selection/7c50e7c95f8d57e8c2cf800424231b37ee9844a3458953ffca6278685bf63459" "q-3612/selection/4483b951f4ebc1f59c02791c83d8c6eb30900b71491c8259ba655efdc2e63d22" "q-3612/selection/ba537c76c05c73718ad3b01ea2b4a74658881a86190c8376c56e2027bb244c7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-3612" :question/id #uuid "b7a5ae82-e9e5-5bd4-bec7-af8bae54592e" :question/math-academy-id "q-3612" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{5{t}^{2}+20t+6}{{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}+t}\\,\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{5{t}^{2}+20t+6}{{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}+t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\frac{5{t}^{2}+20t+6}{t(t+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{t}^{2}+20t+6}{t(t+1)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{t}+\\frac{B}{t+1}+\\frac{C}{(t+1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $t(t+1)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n5{t}^{2}+20t+6=A(t+1)^{2}+B(t)(t+1)+C(t).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $t=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and $C$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(0)^{2}+20(0)+6 & =A(0+1)^{2}+B(0)(0+1)+C(0) \\\\ 6 & =A \\\\ A & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $t=-1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-1)^{2}+20(-1)+6 & =A(-1+1)^{2}+B(-1)(-1+1)+C(-1) \\\\ -9 & =-C \\\\ C & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $t=1$ and substituting the known values of $A$ and $C,$ we can solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)^{2}+20(1)+6 & =A(1+1)^{2}+B(1)(1+1)+C(1) \\\\ 31 & =4A+2B+C \\\\ 31 & =4(6)+2B+(9) \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{t}^{2}+20t+6}{t(t+1)^{2}}=\\frac{6}{t}-\\frac{1}{t+1}+\\frac{9}{(t+1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5{t}^{2}+20t+6}{t(t+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (\\frac{(6)}{t}+\\frac{(-1)}{t+1}+\\frac{(9)}{(t+1)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t-\\int \\frac{1}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t+9\\int \\frac{1}{(t+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t+1|-\\frac{9}{t+1}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-3612/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf7f11d9-6aa8-5922-a5fa-89f7dba66644"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3612"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346752/field-1/0376373e293c918221cca22a934d9604f394d7bcd7f3e56652d650844be523fc" :answer/id #uuid "3197950d-1c10-5e62-b731-ec6f02a394ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(3)-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346752/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1c2579b-cee5-5efa-9281-33c5279a3c71" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346752/field-1/0376373e293c918221cca22a934d9604f394d7bcd7f3e56652d650844be523fc" :answer-field/choices ["q-346752/field-1/0376373e293c918221cca22a934d9604f394d7bcd7f3e56652d650844be523fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346752" :question/id #uuid "1f96ef11-e2cc-5a01-bc43-3b896b801eb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-346752" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{x-4}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}=\\frac{x-4}{(x-1)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{(x-1)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-1)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\nx-4=A(x-1)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-4 & =A(1-1)+B \\\\ B & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0-4 & =A(0-1)+B \\\\ -4 & =-A-3 \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{(x-1)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x-1}-\\frac{3}{(x-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{x-4}{(x-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}(\\frac{1}{x-1}-\\frac{3}{(x-1)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{(x-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|\\,{|}_{2}^{4}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)+3(\\frac{1}{3}-1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{1})+3(-\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-346752/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf7f11d9-6aa8-5922-a5fa-89f7dba66644"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346752"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115623/selection/e7132201d860c875158f61630bb881952e120cb447d6027afa59d8dbb8d1825c" :answer/id #uuid "f3173e69-3a59-5b06-95bd-75454c7963c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\frac{1}{2x+1}+\\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115623/selection/b79da7d999ad5e518d1cf0bb0b9a774756af03fd0f1088065777c42d3ee2d586" :answer/id #uuid "d6fabf61-f9ea-5b30-88ae-98fcf0c2834d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\frac{2}{2x+1}+\\frac{1}{2(2x+1)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115623/selection/c749913ca286e16605493eaae2f476338123a94c8cbe6c5a8e2b15c8f57a14df" :answer/id #uuid "68da6f7b-a9a0-5a37-a1a4-02525bce58ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{1}{4(2x+1)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115623/selection/cf8666afc029c3d83b58c76d9e2f9660b68d96e8f3cb76e0d85e1b65453c2ce6" :answer/id #uuid "e2e43ff4-a13f-5326-8d40-17930e59f4ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\frac{1}{4(2x+1)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115623/selection/7b1683b7b394e19c27ae071467392f2f61a9b812523ff58069ee75d323395eba" :answer/id #uuid "a3d77d3b-592d-5d59-8d9b-4df33ddb1c56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{3}{4(2x+1)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115623/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d78aa3c7-4eef-5807-aeb3-ceb95651772c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115623/selection/c749913ca286e16605493eaae2f476338123a94c8cbe6c5a8e2b15c8f57a14df" :answer-field/choices ["q-115623/selection/e7132201d860c875158f61630bb881952e120cb447d6027afa59d8dbb8d1825c" "q-115623/selection/b79da7d999ad5e518d1cf0bb0b9a774756af03fd0f1088065777c42d3ee2d586" "q-115623/selection/c749913ca286e16605493eaae2f476338123a94c8cbe6c5a8e2b15c8f57a14df" "q-115623/selection/cf8666afc029c3d83b58c76d9e2f9660b68d96e8f3cb76e0d85e1b65453c2ce6" "q-115623/selection/7b1683b7b394e19c27ae071467392f2f61a9b812523ff58069ee75d323395eba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115623" :question/id #uuid "9a7ac9ce-1b80-59f7-acbb-5c7bdeff9908" :question/math-academy-id "q-115623" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{(2x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{(2x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{2x+1}+\\frac{B}{(2x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(2x+1)^{3}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(2x+1)^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}=A(2x+1)^{2}+B(2x+1)+C.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =A{(2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+1)}^{2}+B(2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+1)+C \\\\ 1 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2} & =A(2(0)+1)^{2}+B(2(0)+1)+C \\\\ 0 & =A+B+1 \\\\ A+B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=-1$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-1)^{2} & =A(2(-1)+1)^{2}+B(2(-1)+1)+C \\\\ 4 & =A-B+1 \\\\ A-B & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the equations $A-B=3$ and $A+B=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A & =3-1 \\\\ A & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand substituting back into $A+B=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+B & =-1 \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{(2x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{2}{(2x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{(2x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{2}{(2x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{1}{4(2x+1)^{2}}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-115623/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11647cdd-6315-5718-9425-88f4fb93faa7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115623"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115662/selection/755e48acc77b3df72432f766204c18eb08f5ec6ba4a15017ec11b3a1ff1678d2" :answer/id #uuid "d468051c-3d51-5339-8c2c-fed4d34612a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{x+8}+\\frac{2}{(x+8)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115662/selection/ef2166c34ddf3618ff680a3841b45c84613f884cacf10946e9d7b28db3cafdb2" :answer/id #uuid "7cfe4d16-5d30-5652-a593-5b91c33f1efa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+8|-\\frac{2}{x+8}+\\frac{3}{(x+8)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115662/selection/7f7f58d0d2f9f5f880c620031a4c8427694331130ffb746497d79c7d53373058" :answer/id #uuid "4f7a4346-af38-5afd-9c69-a66ca7659c14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x+8}-\\frac{10}{(x+8)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115662/selection/f99e68c5d396f298285346ced95a7d2625bc5542f59ff85622ff83eb0560e062" :answer/id #uuid "443e5940-84af-5c38-9022-ca957a69305e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x+8}+\\frac{5}{(x+8)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115662/selection/f32357e4c4eb2c618aaf4e716e27aca875fa1095175b160c26110c0546ac76ad" :answer/id #uuid "982a5ad8-b8e5-5ab3-897c-b514b429cba6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+8|-\\frac{1}{x+8}+\\frac{5}{(x+8)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115662/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c34d3c2-565f-5501-a65b-818bacdc77b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115662/selection/f99e68c5d396f298285346ced95a7d2625bc5542f59ff85622ff83eb0560e062" :answer-field/choices ["q-115662/selection/755e48acc77b3df72432f766204c18eb08f5ec6ba4a15017ec11b3a1ff1678d2" "q-115662/selection/ef2166c34ddf3618ff680a3841b45c84613f884cacf10946e9d7b28db3cafdb2" "q-115662/selection/7f7f58d0d2f9f5f880c620031a4c8427694331130ffb746497d79c7d53373058" "q-115662/selection/f99e68c5d396f298285346ced95a7d2625bc5542f59ff85622ff83eb0560e062" "q-115662/selection/f32357e4c4eb2c618aaf4e716e27aca875fa1095175b160c26110c0546ac76ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115662" :question/id #uuid "64afdcef-8011-5961-a509-37f146762065" :question/math-academy-id "q-115662" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{x-2}{(x+8)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{(x+8)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x+8}+\\frac{B}{(x+8)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+8)^{3}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+8)^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\nx-2=A(x+8)^{2}+B(x+8)+C.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-8,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)-2 & =A(-8+8)^{2}+B(-8+8)+C \\\\ -10 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=-7$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-7)-2 & =A(-7+8)^{2}+B(-7+8)+C \\\\ -9 & =A+B-10 \\\\ A+B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=-9$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-9)-2 & =A(-9+8)^{2}+B(-9+8)+C \\\\ -11 & =A-B-10 \\\\ A-B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the equations $A-B=-1$ and $A+B=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A & =-1+1 \\\\ 2A & =0 \\\\ A & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand substituting back into $A+B=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+B & =1 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{(x+8)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{(x+8)^{2}}-\\frac{10}{(x+8)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-2}{(x+8)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{(x+8)^{2}}-\\frac{10}{(x+8)^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x+8)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-10\\int \\frac{1}{(x+8)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x+8}+\\frac{5}{(x+8)^{2}}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-115662/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11647cdd-6315-5718-9425-88f4fb93faa7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115662"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115656/selection/0cb4bcc1a50347699fd3ff882fa496a50266cf2b5ef5bd1ae21faac7de8642e9" :answer/id #uuid "75427d30-f5e4-5518-a8ed-00d59cf98817" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|-\\frac{1}{3(3x+1)}-\\frac{2}{3(3x+1)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115656/selection/75b7556de82e5364acf032b34879fe8feb746497ba8d7de5da30bc720a6933f2" :answer/id #uuid "c65de0c3-a41e-5e27-b84f-d386da59806a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+\\frac{1}{3x+1}+\\frac{2}{3(3x+1)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115656/selection/756d3a4bae6781c9e16620bdf08f23ffb0487c4c5b6a34a7acb8c53279a8a6f0" :answer/id #uuid "f997cad2-6080-5b0e-9ec6-468371ff8f5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+\\frac{2}{3(3x+1)}-\\frac{1}{3(3x+1)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115656/selection/9fadf656e887054d03edb84acc595d3bb72da4af54c1b702faa031360db54feb" :answer/id #uuid "8f2ec2b5-1dff-544b-a42f-48a79c5574b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+\\frac{2}{3x+1}-\\frac{1}{(3x+1)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115656/selection/30f0bbed745dccb7171a7488dce7b448f07d97d61c50b078486f3d8398de4e2d" :answer/id #uuid "c7839d84-98d6-549e-9933-3224deea8ec9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+\\frac{4}{3(3x+1)}-\\frac{2}{3(3x+1)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115656/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d7bcf44-2203-5e38-8439-4840b1e2976b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115656/selection/756d3a4bae6781c9e16620bdf08f23ffb0487c4c5b6a34a7acb8c53279a8a6f0" :answer-field/choices ["q-115656/selection/0cb4bcc1a50347699fd3ff882fa496a50266cf2b5ef5bd1ae21faac7de8642e9" "q-115656/selection/75b7556de82e5364acf032b34879fe8feb746497ba8d7de5da30bc720a6933f2" "q-115656/selection/756d3a4bae6781c9e16620bdf08f23ffb0487c4c5b6a34a7acb8c53279a8a6f0" "q-115656/selection/9fadf656e887054d03edb84acc595d3bb72da4af54c1b702faa031360db54feb" "q-115656/selection/30f0bbed745dccb7171a7488dce7b448f07d97d61c50b078486f3d8398de4e2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115656" :question/id #uuid "03c224d9-3048-59ae-958c-8f685711017c" :question/math-academy-id "q-115656" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{9{x}^{2}+1}{(3x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9{x}^{2}+1}{(3x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{3x+1}+\\frac{B}{(3x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(3x+1)^{3}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(3x+1)^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+1=A(3x+1)^{2}+B(3x+1)+C.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{3},$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+1 & =A{(3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})+1)}^{2}+B(3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})+1)+C \\\\ 2 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(0)^{2}+1 & =A(3(0)+1)^{2}+B(3(0)+1)+C \\\\ 1 & =A+B+2 \\\\ A+B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=-1$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(-1)^{2}+1 & =A(3(-1)+1)^{2}+B(3(-1)+1)+C \\\\ 10 & =4A-2B+2 \\\\ 4A-2B & =8 \\\\ 2A-B & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the equations $2A-B=4$ and $A+B=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3A & =4-1 \\\\ A & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand substituting back into $A+B=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+B & =-1 \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{9{x}^{2}+1}{(3x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{3x+1}-\\frac{2}{(3x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(3x+1)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9{x}^{2}+1}{(3x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{3x+1}-\\frac{2}{(3x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(3x+1)^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{(3x+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{(3x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+\\frac{2}{3(3x+1)}-\\frac{1}{3(3x+1)^{2}}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-115656/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11647cdd-6315-5718-9425-88f4fb93faa7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115656"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-82892"] :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3x+1}{(x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+1}{(x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x+1}+\\frac{B}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)^{3}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+1)^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n3x+1=A(x+1)^{2}+B(x+1)+C.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-1)+1 & =A(-1+1)^{2}+B(-1+1)+C \\\\ -2 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)+1 & =A(0+1)^{2}+B(0+1)+C \\\\ 1 & =A+B-2 \\\\ A+B & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=-2$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-2)+1 & =A(-2+1)^{2}+B(-2+1)+C \\\\ -5 & =A-B-2 \\\\ A-B & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the equations $A-B=-3$ and $A+B=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A & =-3+3 \\\\ 2A & =0 \\\\ A & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand substituting back into $A+B=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+B & =3 \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+1}{(x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{2}}-\\frac{2}{(x+1)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x+1}{(x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{2}}-\\frac{2}{(x+1)^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{(x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{x+1}+\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-115655/selection/66f26947f8283b93a6605ea81ec1513059f8855f14b5a3375a6e64661d1c70bb" :answer/id #uuid "95b294d4-9c65-5ab5-abba-fa64221d7406" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-6|-\\frac{1}{x-6}+\\frac{1}{(x-6)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115655/selection/cf69291afbc9df3853524ee01a598aacb3ca05e476698161f6bfe1d55a7c6186" :answer/id #uuid "0f85775a-5507-5504-ad14-6cfb9faa4a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-6|+\\frac{2}{x-6}-\\frac{3}{(x-6)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115655/selection/6a12aa5cbfa6996b60f03576b1eb2d8d777d9140183af6de677d29dc79810fd2" :answer/id #uuid "b47d9eb7-7154-52d6-84b7-5d7579de0a0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-6|+\\frac{2}{x-6}+\\frac{4}{(x-6)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115655/selection/04353594bb4227e5b70dc66157bd1ee7d857b3e88fed3cc20701c679a4889725" :answer/id #uuid "c254d3a6-b98d-537f-81a7-bdb3e3f71dbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-6|-\\frac{3}{x-6}-\\frac{2}{(x-6)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115655/selection/b129b587d1c9599a26a25f82b063d305f2d5405df19bfaa8619afbb529360916" :answer/id #uuid "543a1e7f-f6f2-5988-8f27-3dba6c473604" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-6|+\\frac{3}{x-6}-\\frac{1}{(x-6)^{2}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115655/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ad9f03e-f0e3-5b26-a221-402db58f9c7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115655/selection/b129b587d1c9599a26a25f82b063d305f2d5405df19bfaa8619afbb529360916" :answer-field/choices ["q-115655/selection/66f26947f8283b93a6605ea81ec1513059f8855f14b5a3375a6e64661d1c70bb" "q-115655/selection/cf69291afbc9df3853524ee01a598aacb3ca05e476698161f6bfe1d55a7c6186" "q-115655/selection/6a12aa5cbfa6996b60f03576b1eb2d8d777d9140183af6de677d29dc79810fd2" "q-115655/selection/04353594bb4227e5b70dc66157bd1ee7d857b3e88fed3cc20701c679a4889725" "q-115655/selection/b129b587d1c9599a26a25f82b063d305f2d5405df19bfaa8619afbb529360916"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115655" :question/id #uuid "563e16e6-d669-5850-92a8-f4c65daa5805" :question/math-academy-id "q-115655" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{-{x}^{2}+9x-16}{(x-6)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{-{x}^{2}+9x-16}{(x-6)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-6}+\\frac{B}{(x-6)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-6)^{3}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-6)^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+9x-16=A(x-6)^{2}+B(x-6)+C.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=6,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(6)^{2}+9(6)-16 & =A(6-6)^{2}+B(6-6)+C \\\\ 2 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=5$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(5)^{2}+9(5)-16 & =A(5-6)^{2}+B(5-6)+C \\\\ 4 & =A-B+2 \\\\ A-B & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=7$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(7)^{2}+9(7)-16 & =A(7-6)^{2}+B(7-6)+C \\\\ -2 & =A+B+2 \\\\ A+B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the equations $A-B=2$ and $A+B=-4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A & =2-4 \\\\ A & =-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nand substituting back into $A+B=-4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1+B & =-4 \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{-{x}^{2}+9x-16}{(x-5)^{3}}=-\\frac{1}{x-6}-\\frac{3}{(x-6)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x-6)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-{x}^{2}+9x-16}{(x-6)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{1}{x-6}-\\frac{3}{(x-6)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(x-6)^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x-6}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{(x-6)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{(x-6)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-6|+\\frac{3}{x-6}-\\frac{1}{(x-6)^{2}}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-115655/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11647cdd-6315-5718-9425-88f4fb93faa7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115655"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-508"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 \\dfrac{2x+3}{(x+1)^2} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x+3}{(x+1)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{(x+1)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x+1)^2}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+1)^2$ and get\n\n$$\n2x+3 = A(x+1)+B .\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)+3 & =A(-1+1)+B \\\\ 1 & =0+B \\\\ B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)+3 & =A(0+1)+B \\\\ 3 & =A+B \\\\ 3 & =A+1 \\\\ A & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x+3}{(x+1)^2} = \\dfrac{2}{(x+1)} +\\dfrac{1}{(x+1)^2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2x+3}{(x+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{2}{(x+1)}+\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1||}_{0}^{1}+{(-\\frac{1}{x+1})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1||}_{0}^{1}-{\\frac{1}{x+1}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1]-[\\frac{1}{2}-1] \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7298"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)}\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}-5x+8}{(x-3)^{2}(x+1)} & =\\frac{A}{(x-3)}+\\frac{B}{(x-3)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-3)^2(x+1)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-5x+8 & =A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+1)+C(x-3)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $C$ and solve for $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({3}^{2})-5(3)+8 & =A(3-3)(3+1)+B(3+1)+C(3-3)^{2} \\\\ 20 & =B(4) \\\\ B & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-1)^{2}-5(-1)+8 & =A(-1-3)(-1+1)+B(-1+1)+C(-1-3)^{2} \\\\ 16 & =C{(-4)}^{2} \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known values of $B$ and $C,$ we can solve for $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({0}^{2})-5(0)+8 & =A(0-3)(0+1)+B(0+1)+C(0-3)^{2} \\\\ 8 & =-3A+B+9C \\\\ 8 & =-3A+5+9(1) \\\\ 3A & =6 \\\\ A & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)} = \\dfrac{2}{(x-3)} +\\dfrac{5}{(x-3)^2} +\\dfrac{1}{(x+1)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-5x+8}{(x-3)^{2}(x+1)}\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{(x-3)}+\\frac{5}{(x-3)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(x+1)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\text{d}x+5\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}}\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+5(-\\,\\frac{1}{x-3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|-\\frac{5}{(x-3)}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7275"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1} \\dfrac{x}{x^2+2x+1} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{x^2+2x+1} = \\dfrac{x}{(x+1)^2}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{(x+1)^2} = \\dfrac {A}{x+1} + \\dfrac {B}{(x+1)^2}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+1)^2$ and get\n\n$$\nx= A(x+1)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =A(-1+1)+B \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =A(0+1)+B \\\\ 0 & =A+B \\\\ 0 & =A-1 \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{(x+1)^2} = \\dfrac {1}{x+1} - \\dfrac {1}{(x+1)^2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{x+1}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|{|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{1}{x+1}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+1|)+(\\frac{1}{1+1}-\\frac{1}{0+1}) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)+(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-509"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{9x^2+2x-1}{(3x-1)^3}\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9{x}^{2}+2x-1}{(3x-1)^{3}} & =\\frac{A}{(3x-1)}+\\frac{B}{(3x-1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(3x-1)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(3x-1)^3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+2x-1 & =A(3x-1)^{2}+B(3x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=\\dfrac{1}{3},$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+2(\\frac{1}{3})-1 & =A{(3(\\frac{1}{3})-1)}^{2}+B(3(\\frac{1}{3})-1)+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{(0)}^{2}+2(0)-1 & =A{(0-1)}^{2}+B(0-1)+C \\\\ -1 & =A-B+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ A-B & =-\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get another equation relating $A$ and $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{(1)}^{2}+2(1)-1 & =A{(3(1)-1)}^{2}+B(3(1)-1)+C \\\\ 10 & =4A+2B+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 2A+B & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding our two equations $A-B=-\\dfrac{5}{3}$ and $2A+B=\\dfrac{14}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3A & =-\\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{14}{3} \\\\ 3A & =3 \\\\ A & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand substituting back into $2A+B=\\dfrac{14}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)+B & =\\frac{14}{3} \\\\ B & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{9x^2+2x-1}{(3x-1)^3} = \\dfrac{1}{(3x-1)} +\\dfrac{8}{3(3x-1)^2} + \\dfrac{2}{3(3x-1)^3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9{x}^{2}+2x-1}{(3x-1)^{3}}\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{(3x-1)}+\\frac{8}{3(3x-1)^{2}}+\\frac{2}{3(3x-1)^{3}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{3x-1}\\text{d}x+\\frac{8}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{(3x-1)^{2}}\\text{d}x+\\frac{2}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{(3x-1)^{3}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-1|+\\frac{8}{3}(-\\,\\frac{1}{3(3x-1)})+\\frac{2}{3}(-\\,\\frac{1}{6(3x-1)^{2}})+K \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-1|-\\frac{8}{9(3x-1)}-\\frac{1}{9(3x-1)^{2}}+K\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
